<body>
    <h1>Azure DevOps Integration</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <h1 local-id=3D"9bb594df-dc97-48fb-9e54-8e9845f8e102" id=3D"AzureDe=
vOpsIntegration-ConnecttoAzurewithanAzureResourceManagerserviceconnection">=
Connect to Azure with an Azure Resource Manager service connection</h1>
<p local-id=3D"3ff4cba8-84fe-43e1-bd20-9e0c9d24a951"></p>
<p local-id=3D"3ff4cba8-84fe-43e1-bd20-9e0c9d24a951"><strong>Azure DevOps S=
ervices | Azure DevOps Server | Azure DevOps Server 2022</strong></p>
<p local-id=3D"ff0d25ee-beea-4732-8639-c22761a1b0c8">An Azure Resource Mana=
ger service connection allows you to connect to Azure resources like Azure =
Key Vault from your pipeline. This connection lets you use a pipeline to de=
ploy to Azure resources, such as an Azure App Service app, without needing =
to authenticate each time.</p>
<p local-id=3D"a760b417-834e-4861-a5a7-5949d92b1f03">For Dynamics 365 Pipel=
ine Deployment the authentication type used is</p>
<ul local-id=3D"aba9eb61-4103-4097-a227-0b585919bace">
<li local-id=3D"3c6d3122-9230-474c-8960-208992445603">
<p local-id=3D"5644bed1-a85a-4035-b755-e2a3432966ce">User Assigned Managed =
identity that creates a workload identity federation credential.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h2 local-id=3D"b37558c8-9e64-42ad-b7f4-f3f9c7e175cf" id=3D"AzureDevOpsInte=
gration-Createauser-assignedmanagedidentity">Create a user-assigned managed=
 identity</h2>
<p local-id=3D"2c021fec-3c83-47fe-8ad9-e4f2f241cad7"><a class=3D"external-l=
ink" href=3D"https://btsprod.service-now.com/sp?id=3Dticket&amp;table=3Dsc_=
req_item&amp;sys_id=3Ddfcf063d47a276909ad38571516d4373&amp;view=3Dsp" rel=
=3D"nofollow">RITM2238685 - Service Portal</a></p>
<p local-id=3D"f4c6c3ba-2191-4b00-a01e-30d94f906959"><span class=3D"conflue=
nce-jim-macro jira-issue resolved" data-jira-key=3D"MATT-13709"> <a href=3D=
"https://wrberkley.atlassian.net/browse/MATT-13709" class=3D"jira-issue-key=
"><img class=3D"icon" src=3D"https://wrberkley.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/uni=
versal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10616?size=3Dmedium">MATT-13709</a=
> - <span class=3D"summary">Provision and Deploy Managed Identities for eac=
h Environment</span> <span class=3D"aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-subtle aui-loze=
nge-success jira-macro-single-issue-export-pdf">Closed</span> </span></p>
<p local-id=3D"2db1700a-7307-49b8-9047-2ec19da17033">To create a user-assig=
ned managed identity, your account needs the <a class=3D"external-link" hre=
f=3D"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/role-based-access-control/buil=
t-in-roles#managed-identity-contributor" rel=3D"nofollow">Managed Identity =
Contributor</a> role assignment.</p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"bd64716d-b077-4dcc-bb6f-510f923c4c2c">
<li local-id=3D"1837b37c-f905-4716-9b7e-8fa0484c61ea">
<p local-id=3D"1713f2f6-99f2-4c02-9d75-ce5cb64c4e4c">Sign in to the <a clas=
s=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://portal.azure.com/" rel=3D"nofollow">Azu=
re portal</a>.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"55dc99a7-c97f-4c08-a7ba-1190dd915440">
<p local-id=3D"4afbeff9-f807-465d-89a5-4b2c156b64fa">In the search box, ent=
er <strong>Managed Identities</strong>. Under <strong>Services</strong>, se=
lect <strong>Managed Identities</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"7d7c4887-20fe-4762-af8b-557a87981a69">
<p local-id=3D"48fcac1f-4f15-4406-9f60-1ae7c47395bf">Select <strong>Add</st=
rong>, and enter values in the following boxes in the <strong>Create User A=
ssigned Managed Identity</strong> pane:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"6d888fa4-7715-451c-8d48-5fe872d939f5">
<li local-id=3D"ed49757a-70f5-4c6e-b84b-c9202846727c">
<p local-id=3D"f4be716c-3681-44d2-92d9-9b3f3c7d411e"><strong>Subscription</=
strong>: Choose the subscription to create the user-assigned managed identi=
ty under.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"c43b2d26-623b-4e8c-98ec-3c071740b9d9">
<p local-id=3D"5e9d5afb-8690-4900-b442-705347e1a0a5"><strong>Resource group=
</strong>: Choose a resource group to create the user-assigned managed iden=
tity in, or select <strong>Create new</strong> to create a new resource gro=
up.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"ddd2448f-dd05-4a80-a58e-6697f198e6f3">
<p local-id=3D"ed85b8e2-b23c-481d-8ce9-fadf5107e057"><strong>Region</strong=
>: Choose a region to deploy the user-assigned managed identity, for exampl=
e, <strong>West US</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"dad606b1-fb05-4f2c-9cf9-c21152092185">
<p local-id=3D"ddffde66-676c-4e57-96e2-ad9d2a944b92"><strong>Name</strong>:=
 Enter the name for your user-assigned managed identity, for example, UAI1.=
</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"670fddde-b4a7-42ef-ab6a-739279cb1ea6">Important</p>
<p local-id=3D"6a2e4d9b-b1bb-4e7d-984e-68961ede6fda">When you create user-a=
ssigned managed identities, the name must start with a letter or number, an=
d may include a combination of alphanumeric characters, hyphens (-) and und=
erscores (_). For the assignment to a virtual machine or virtual machine sc=
ale set to work properly, the name is limited to 24 characters. For more in=
formation, see <a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://learn.microsoft.c=
om/en-us/entra/identity/managed-identities-azure-resources/known-issues" re=
l=3D"nofollow"><u>FAQs and known issues</u></a>.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"1d6c9eec-7638-41fc-a1c5-db57eb2a64ef">
<p local-id=3D"1a9c060c-e3f0-4b99-849a-468516536362">Select <strong>Review =
+ create</strong> to review the changes.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"59c326de-ea0f-4a40-8035-6b1c6eb784fa">
<p local-id=3D"51e4b1d8-bfbe-4c0e-8b16-6f880701a58e">Select <strong>Create<=
/strong>.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper image-center-wrapper conflu=
ence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image confluen=
ce-external-resource image-center" alt=3D"Screenshot that shows the Create =
User Assigned Managed Identity pane." width=3D"692" src=3D"https://learn.mi=
crosoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/managed-identities-azure-resources/media/h=
ow-manage-user-assigned-managed-identities/create-user-assigned-managed-ide=
ntity-portal.png" data-image-src=3D"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra=
/identity/managed-identities-azure-resources/media/how-manage-user-assigned=
-managed-identities/create-user-assigned-managed-identity-portal.png" loadi=
ng=3D"lazy"></span>
<p local-id=3D"41c6f893-29f3-4fb9-b1d8-f7b36e23cfc0"></p>
<span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper image-center-wrapper conflu=
ence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image image-ce=
nter" alt=3D"image-20260122-201255.png" width=3D"468" loading=3D"lazy" src=
=3D"bdfd19b5a9d1c734be12e4facb1598d375307bcefb98219a3a51fed53b845698" data-=
image-src=3D"https://wrberkley.atlassian.net/wiki/download/attachments/1580=
498969/image-20260122-201255.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1769112=
779372&amp;cacheVersion=3D1&amp;api=3Dv2" data-height=3D"498" data-width=3D=
"1076" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"15816=
78616" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"atta=
chment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"image-20260122-201255.png" da=
ta-base-url=3D"https://wrberkley.atlassian.net/wiki" data-linked-resource-c=
ontent-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"1580498969" =
data-linked-resource-container-version=3D"3" data-media-id=3D"c953a52e-3dce=
-4a01-abc5-4869e275f066" data-media-type=3D"file" height=3D"216"></span>
<h2 local-id=3D"e8fc834a-458b-4213-95ba-e5fdb80d9d15" id=3D"AzureDevOpsInte=
gration-Manageaccesstouser-assignedmanagedidentities">Manage access to user=
-assigned managed identities</h2>
<p local-id=3D"491f2d0b-faf8-45fc-b23d-b4fcc86d98ea">In some environments, =
administrators choose to limit who can manage user-assigned managed identit=
ies. Administrators can implement this limitation using <a class=3D"externa=
l-link" href=3D"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/role-based-access-c=
ontrol/built-in-roles#identity" rel=3D"nofollow">built-in</a> RBAC roles. Y=
ou can use these roles to grant a user or group in your organization rights=
 over a user-assigned managed identity.</p>
<span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper image-center-wrapper conflu=
ence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image image-ce=
nter" alt=3D"image-20260122-201539.png" width=3D"468" loading=3D"lazy" src=
=3D"bc3981171fea8f8ee75bcc4d27a712ba8dec4d7ecd3e0586ea40ac9338fc7cba" data-=
image-src=3D"https://wrberkley.atlassian.net/wiki/download/attachments/1580=
498969/image-20260122-201539.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1769112=
942046&amp;cacheVersion=3D1&amp;api=3Dv2" data-height=3D"486" data-width=3D=
"935" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"157990=
9162" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attac=
hment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"image-20260122-201539.png" dat=
a-base-url=3D"https://wrberkley.atlassian.net/wiki" data-linked-resource-co=
ntent-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"1580498969" d=
ata-linked-resource-container-version=3D"3" data-media-id=3D"449ef7d1-6095-=
4472-b95f-620760024efd" data-media-type=3D"file" height=3D"243"></span>
<p local-id=3D"611e71c9-52db-4ce3-b89d-965515d194fd"></p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"1ec84e21-324a-4b20-b4bc-c9de986d769d">
<li local-id=3D"1d550bfc-46ed-4586-9440-7cecae485594">
<p local-id=3D"6871f8cf-61a4-4d91-ad43-84a70d5d5ada">Sign in to the <a clas=
s=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://portal.azure.com/" rel=3D"nofollow">Azu=
re portal</a>.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"051fc7d8-60f3-4c0c-bb83-599d90534657">
<p local-id=3D"29f5fdb1-de6f-4819-a6e2-3d9a80a5b360">In the search box, ent=
er <strong>Managed Identities</strong>. Under <strong>Services</strong>, se=
lect <strong>Managed Identities</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"8a6e6a98-ab41-45c6-ab1c-a9bf86f4d574">
<p local-id=3D"82e1dabf-d89a-4b5f-8416-53a48a2fab64">A list of the user-ass=
igned managed identities for your subscription is returned. Select the user=
-assigned managed identity that you want to manage.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"e301617b-d0ae-4f96-8a16-e152612803e5">
<p local-id=3D"40e248ab-a0e7-4501-b19f-7e7ddcd9e128">Select <strong>Access =
control (IAM)</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"efea8fdc-1800-4118-bc6f-d46893bdeb4b">
<p local-id=3D"09794c53-146f-4610-907f-df5829664969">Choose <strong>Add rol=
e assignment</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"93824dac-adc5-46b4-beed-238368e74017">
<p local-id=3D"812539a7-7d44-45c6-ad46-5ce3d043bc7e">In the <strong>Add rol=
e assignment</strong> pane, choose the role to assign and choose <strong>Ne=
xt</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"a785be5e-c123-4aa2-9884-a3d4f5c54369">
<p local-id=3D"00bc5c25-9dad-40dc-8c6e-1cafe52970f9">Choose who should have=
 the role assigned.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<h2 local-id=3D"af6002e6-8446-4ae8-ac74-017ae7338681" id=3D"AzureDevOpsInte=
gration-Createaserviceconnectionforanexistinguser-assignedmanagedidentity">=
Create a service connection for an existing user-assigned managed identity<=
/h2>
<p local-id=3D"645ee873-5331-4fcb-b64a-22ccea8fc69d">Use this option to aut=
omatically create a workload identity credential for an existing user-assig=
ned managed identity. You need to have an <a class=3D"external-link" href=
=3D"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/managed-identities-azu=
re-resources/how-manage-user-assigned-managed-identities?pivots=3Didentity-=
mi-methods-azp#create-a-user-assigned-managed-identity" rel=3D"nofollow">ex=
isting user-assigned managed identity</a> before you start.</p>
<span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper image-center-wrapper conflu=
ence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image confluen=
ce-external-resource image-center" alt=3D"Screenshot that shows choosing Az=
ure Resource Manager selection." width=3D"250" src=3D"https://learn.microso=
ft.com/en-us/azure/devops/pipelines/library/media/new-service-connection-az=
ure-resource-manager.png?view=3Dazure-devops" data-image-src=3D"https://lea=
rn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/pipelines/library/media/new-service-con=
nection-azure-resource-manager.png?view=3Dazure-devops" loading=3D"lazy"></=
span><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper image-center-wrapper c=
onfluence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image con=
fluence-external-resource image-center" alt=3D"Screenshot that shows choosi=
ng Azure Resource Manager selection of managed identity with user assigned =
identity." width=3D"250" src=3D"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/dev=
ops/pipelines/library/media/azure-resource-manager-options-managed-identity=
.png?view=3Dazure-devops" data-image-src=3D"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-=
us/azure/devops/pipelines/library/media/azure-resource-manager-options-mana=
ged-identity.png?view=3Dazure-devops" loading=3D"lazy"></span>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"7a847459-e8a1-44f8-b19b-837bf42285a1">
<li local-id=3D"3d70fecc-793a-47a4-9f65-96fe4c65c855">
<p local-id=3D"37de4d3e-d029-4ae7-aecc-db5ecb1b51f8">In the Azure DevOps pr=
oject, go to <strong>Project settings</strong> &gt; <strong>Service connect=
ions</strong>.</p>
<p local-id=3D"e4304207-f2ea-4d91-8267-5fdcd720531c">For more information, =
see <a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/az=
ure/devops/project/navigation/go-to-service-page?view=3Dazure-devops#open-p=
roject-settings" rel=3D"nofollow">Open project settings</a>.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"7199c853-6725-453a-bc35-be946e2bec52">
<p local-id=3D"eefcb20f-8f3a-44da-97bd-164656f6a961">Select <strong>New ser=
vice connection</strong>, select <strong>Resource Manager</strong>, and sel=
ect <strong>Next</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"85f3b85a-8909-4215-a4ec-d6417b9c8990">
<p local-id=3D"f4651ed7-4686-4834-bf1e-59f3394e5e22">Select <strong>Managed=
 identity</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"730a805e-2217-4e8a-b87a-3b232f06108b">
<p local-id=3D"6e87e095-3663-46d2-8789-7988587ac0e8">In <strong>Step 1: Man=
aged identity details</strong>:</p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"777cf840-bc1f-4150-a203-0abb2907ebb2">
<li local-id=3D"eb198342-10e5-4555-b1ac-8b83a32525d8">
<p local-id=3D"3883f847-cc38-433c-aae3-bf1f6bee4edf">Select <strong>Subscri=
ption for Managed Identity</strong>. This is the Azure subscription that co=
ntains your managed identity.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"3bf7c3bc-377d-48e0-b18e-904998f6cb3a">
<p local-id=3D"8b3ab689-d5c2-4c5f-9dd9-64ab3dcae026">Select <strong>Resourc=
e group for Managed Identity</strong>. This is the resource group that cont=
ains your managed identity.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"f5ffa286-e2ea-4431-b0fb-5155bd73b638">
<p local-id=3D"ba68bb57-3117-4638-9c23-60b7b5685cf7">Select <strong>Managed=
 Identity</strong>. This is the managed identity within your resource group=
 that you use to access resources.</p>
</li>
</ol>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"f612311a-0a95-4a2a-9a34-0a9ed413fc63">
<p local-id=3D"85b43b82-2fa0-417c-8f78-f8c6c0aeac25">In <strong>Step 2: Azu=
re Scope</strong>:</p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"b3de0360-19ab-4593-b987-d8c7c57ad597">
<li local-id=3D"51118221-3c31-428b-b887-0e50fe227def">
<p local-id=3D"2fcc37e3-1cc5-4a0c-a2c7-bc82d4212eed">Select the <strong>Sco=
pe Level</strong>. Select <strong>Subscription</strong>, <strong>Management=
 Group</strong>, or <strong>Machine Learning Workspace</strong>. <a class=
=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-re=
source-manager/management-groups-overview" rel=3D"nofollow">Management grou=
ps</a> are containers that help you manage access, policy, and compliance a=
cross multiple subscriptions. A <a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://=
learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/machine-learning/concept-workspace" rel=3D"=
nofollow">Machine Learning Workspace</a> is place to create machine learnin=
g artifacts.</p>
<ul local-id=3D"f5dd266e-eada-472b-9c74-e287c88edb81">
<li local-id=3D"f0727a5e-52b2-4567-9683-25e29378d021">
<p local-id=3D"af0d96df-48ae-466b-9273-ab56d1e205bb">For the <strong>Subscr=
iption</strong> scope, enter the following parameters:</p>
<p local-id=3D"dcbd8bf8-478d-4372-99bf-b51213aa20d8">ParameterDescription<s=
trong>Subscription for service connection</strong>Required. Select the Azur=
e subscription name your managed identity accesses.<strong>Resource group f=
or service connection</strong>Optional. Enter to limit managed identity acc=
ess to one resource group.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"b1862ac1-f6af-4714-99d9-b7597e3c337d">
<p local-id=3D"4f827ed0-7784-41e0-bd5e-763bbc01c133">For the <strong>Manage=
ment Group</strong> scope, enter the following parameters:</p>
<p local-id=3D"ecde5f8e-891a-4eb0-902b-6c9cee67b594">ParameterDescription<s=
trong>Management Group</strong>Required. Select the Azure management group.=
</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"8d909657-6777-4db6-8746-f141c8e88b27">
<p local-id=3D"f56661e0-56bb-4e52-a394-04ec42fe6bff">For the <strong>Machin=
e Learning Workspace</strong> scope, enter the following parameters:</p>
<p local-id=3D"277a2b60-8915-4449-b93a-41173c9a701b">ParameterDescription<s=
trong>Subscription</strong>Required. Select the Azure subscription name.<st=
rong>Resource group for service connection</strong>Optional. Select the res=
ource group containing the workspace.<strong>ML Workspace workspace</strong=
>Required. Enter the name of the existing Azure Machine Learning workspace.=
</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"23225d06-1bff-4e06-81de-724dfe5a83cb">
<p local-id=3D"9c6bd417-0b32-4b06-bd63-c0413af2fdb0">In the <strong>Step 3:=
 Service connection details:</strong> section, enter or select the followin=
g parameters:</p>
<p local-id=3D"6f0966e3-6870-4048-a7b1-a1ef0fc903dd">ParameterDescription<s=
trong>Service Connection Name</strong>Required. The name that you use to re=
fer to this service connection in task properties. Not the name of your Azu=
re subscription.<strong>Service Management Reference</strong>Optional. Cont=
ext information from an ITSM database.<strong>Description</strong>Optional.=
 Enter a description of the service connection.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"12fe0ba6-ddb4-4796-8b50-7238a7750cd2">
<p local-id=3D"436d981f-09c0-4112-a649-3f1ee5299700">In the <strong>Securit=
y</strong> section, select <strong>Grant access permission to all pipelines=
</strong> to allow all pipelines to use this service connection. If you don=
't select this option, you must manually grant access to each pipeline that=
 uses this service connection.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"43ae79d9-346c-49f0-8891-790dd3cc2ba1">
<p local-id=3D"c7011d04-21f1-4085-914c-0705c60e18c1">Make sure to grant acc=
ess to the Resource Groups and the storage containers.</p>
</li>
<li local-id=3D"948c70ca-d796-4e2a-93c6-16bf24402325">
<p local-id=3D"b39550c8-afbf-485c-944c-a3a0bfd8cf8c">Select <strong>Save</s=
trong> to validate and create the service connection.</p>
</li>
</ol>
</li>
</ol>
<p local-id=3D"d24dc924-5b73-4d70-852c-ac1e8eb1e591"><span class=3D"conflue=
nce-embedded-file-wrapper image-center-wrapper confluence-embedded-manual-s=
ize"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image image-center" alt=3D"image-202=
60122-201839.png" width=3D"468" loading=3D"lazy" src=3D"005962972e16b305af7=
e020f9238cac257d5a0061a01889a7992fd1a7c96356d" data-image-src=3D"https://wr=
berkley.atlassian.net/wiki/download/attachments/1580498969/image-20260122-2=
01839.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1769113121244&amp;cacheVersion=
